 "text": "Montgomery County, OH - Official Website | Official Website\nSkip to Main Content\nCreate a Website Account - Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.\nWebsite Sign In\nSearch\nGovernment\nDepartments\nResidents\nBusiness\nVisitors\nI Want To\nCareers\nResident Services\nTaxes\nElections\nAuditor\nTransparency\nWelcome to\nThe Birthplace of Innovation\nFind what you need\nPopular Services\nEmployee Benefits\nSurplus Property Auction\nSupplier Services\nPublic Record Request\nOnline Bids\nDomestic Violence\nChildren Services\nJob & Family Services\nSenior Services\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nMontgomery County\nVideo Tour\nTour Chapters ▼\nWelcome\nEconomic Development\nWorkforce\nArts and Culture\nHuman and Public Services\nFamily Entertainment\nLatest\nCounty News\nMontgomery County Marks Progress Toward New Job and Training Center\nMontgomery County is marking a major step forward in plans for a new Job and Training Center in Harrison Township as the county moves from property acquisition into design and planning for the $40 million project. Read on...\nNew SafetyNet Portal Strengthens Behavioral Health Coordination Across Montgomery County\nA new SafetyNet Portal is helping organizations across Montgomery County’s behavioral health continuum of care better coordinate services and connect residents with the care and support they need. Read on...\nMontgomery County Launches Enhanced Emergency Alert System to Keep Residents Informed and Safe\nMontgomery County’s Emergency Management Agency has launched a new emergency alert Mass Notification System, powered by Regroup, to keep residents informed and safe during emergency situations. Read on...\nMontgomery County’s Opioid Settlement Investment Reaches More Than 6,500 People\nMontgomery County is highlighting the results of its more than $2 million investment in 13 local nonprofits through the Direct Opioid Settlement Funding Opportunity Community Impact Report. Read on...\nView All News\n/CivicAlerts.aspx\nCounty Administration Building\n451 West Third Street\nDayton, OH 45422\nHome\nSite Map\nContact Us\nAccessibility\nCopyright Notices\nPrivacy Policy\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nGovernment Websites by CivicPlus®\nLoading\nLoading\nDo Not Show Again\nClose\n[]\nClose ×",
